  {
   "k": "kftl9b",
   "en": "Release Welsh Argentina and play as them (don't forget to uncheck \"release as puppet\"!). Build an early heavy ship with at least 375 naval supremacy. An early heavy ship without any modules should suffice but does need 4000 manpower. Additionally youll need at least 4 Convoys to move your troops to England. You will likely need to rejoin your original faction in order to naval-invade Wales from any nearby country, since the game won't let you plan a naval invasion from an unrelated country even if you have military access. For that, you'll need to switch ideology, since Welsh Argentina starts non-aligned. E.g., if doing this after \"Bad Ending\", you'll need to go communist. (You can try to work around this somehow, since switching ideology takes a long time.) One additional wrinkle is that, after a sufficiently long and bloody conquest as Brazil or Argentina, your Welsh Argentina cores may have a population deficit. Meaning that you must either wait for the population to regenerate or set the conscription law to \"Service By Requirement\" just to get 20K manpower in the field. As a non-aligned nation, you can't raise conscription above \"Limited Conscription\" unless you're at war. Wales has more than twice your core population and may easily have 40K or more manpower by the time you're done justifying on them. In that case, you'll also want to go fascist/communist. Make a naval invasion to Wales, don't call in any allies! Declare and get that Welsh booty!"
  },
